    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0496" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v22/pg468"/>

                <head>262. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Iran<anchor n="1" xml:id="d262-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1968-03-05T01:23:00+00:00">March 5, 1968,
                    0123Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>124569. Eyes Only for Ambassador. For Ambassador from Under Secretary Rostow. We
                    are concerned about the atmosphere and the implications of these charges and
                    rumors. On their face, they are absurd. But what do they mean? We want not
                    simply the factual ammunition required by the situation but your full evaluation
                    of what these demarches represent, and your advice on how they should be
                    handled. Needless to add, we do not take these transparent attempts to drive
                    wedges seriously. But how serious are the suspicions and fears they
                    represent?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">
                            Rusk
                        </hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
